        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): generate gateway protocol models",
        "body": "Closes #105960\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid hand-maintains gateway frame models, protocol versions, method names, event names, capabilities, and command constants. That surface can drift from the canonical TypeBox protocol and from the generated Swift client.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a Kotlin generator that reads the canonical gateway schemas, core method descriptors, and event coverage source, then emits the Android models and catalogs the app currently consumes. Android keeps its existing kotlinx.serialization stack and shipped structured-params compatibility; a package script provides generated-file drift checks without introducing a second hand-maintained path.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo direct UI change. Android protocol updates now follow the canonical gateway definitions instead of requiring manual model and constant edits.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxd09x8eh7rwgz93ntdcb8ry` ([run 29227218734](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29227218734)): Kotlin generation was byte-for-byte deterministic after regeneration.\n- `pnpm android:lint`\n- `./gradlew :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.gateway.GatewayProtocolGeneratedTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.protocol.OpenClawProtocolConstantsTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.gateway.GatewaySessionInvokeTest`\n- `node scripts/check-protocol-event-coverage.mjs`\n- `pnpm native:i18n:check`\n- `pnpm test test/scripts/check-protocol-event-coverage.test.ts`\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxd0ykhm1d91qnvnkygax3bj` ([run 29227689910](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29227689910)): `pnpm check:test-types` and the 12 focused coverage-extractor tests passed after the declaration-surface fix.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxd221vb0hwyty3gpcwgadcv`: targeted oxfmt/oxlint, `pnpm check:test-types`, Kotlin drift generation, and 12 focused extractor tests passed for the final CI repair.\n- Final formatted-bundle autoreview: no accepted or actionable findings (0.98 confidence).\n",
